  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="30a8389b-44b4-5b74-b99b-3ccedb181c7d" activityNameId="229848b1-eaa3-559e-b492-0ace73cb1284" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Nuclear fuel fabrication plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Nuclear fuel fabrication plant
Data on the construction of a UO2 (no MOX mixed oxides, no RepU reprocessed fuel, and no HEU highly enriched uranium from warheads) fuel fabrication facility are pretty old and representing reference plants form US Studies on total material &amp; energy use in energy chains. It is roughly assumed that 100% of concrete with reinforcing bars are dumped in an depository for inerts.;
UUID: 4f2a68de-e47f-34b7-bbea-9c1cc021b301
The module includes: land use of the factory; energy (electricity and diesel) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled.
Location: North American and European conditions
Technology: Information regards facilities operating in the 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4f2a68de-e47f-34b7-bbea-9c1cc021b301.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
